    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84c22986_af6966fb",
        "filename": "board/cr50/tpm2/virtual_nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 133,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-12T16:50:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "do we expect non-consecutive indices? if not, we can just save on index and implement the table for [virtual_nv_index - VIRTUAL_NV_INDEX_START] and just jump to the right place in table w/o searching through it? if we ever deprecate an old index we can just replace get_data_fn and size for it with 0. if we define 4 indexes and then deprecate one, with this code we\u0027d have a table of 3*(4+4+4) \u003d 36 bytes, and if we drop handles but zero out deprecated we\u0027d have 4 * (4+4) \u003d 32 bytes. and indexing will be faster.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 133,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 133,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "9ea0a4c27935bdf895a6fa9644b3e42fd9060c2d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d878ec83_c2923ba7",
        "filename": "board/cr50/tpm2/virtual_nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 133,
